    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0544" n="450" xml:id="pg450"/>

                <head>No. 301.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Phelps</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 8,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 470.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to instruction No. 466, of
                    the 7th instant, concerning the case of the American fishing schooner <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Molly Adams</hi>, I now transmit to you herewith, for
                    your further information, a copy of the letter<anchor n="*" xml:id="d301-f1"/>
                    of Mr. Solomon Jacobs, of the 12th ultimo, in which the matter was brought to
                    the attention of the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. BAYARD.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
